# 1️⃣ Queue using Array

## 📖 Idea

Store queue elements in an array.

Maintain two indices:

```
Front

Rear
```

---

### Visualization

```
Front                 Rear

↓

10 20 30 40

               ↑
```

---

### Operations

```
Enqueue

↓

Insert at Rear
```

```
Dequeue

↓

Remove from Front
```

---

### C++ Implementation

```cpp
class Queue
{
    int arr[100];
    int front, rear;

public:

    Queue()
    {
        front = 0;
        rear = -1;
    }

    void enqueue(int x)
    {
        arr[++rear] = x;
    }

    void dequeue()
    {
        if(front <= rear)
            front++;
    }

    int Front()
    {
        return arr[front];
    }
};
```

---

### Complexity

| Operation | Time |
|-----------|------|
| Enqueue | O(1) |
| Dequeue | O(1) |

