# 5️⃣ Priority Queue

## 📖 Definition

A Priority Queue removes elements according to their **priority**, not their insertion order.

---

### Example

Input

```
10

5

20

1
```

Output

```
20

10

5

1
```

(Max Heap)

---

### Min Priority Queue

Output

```
1

5

10

20
```

---

### STL Syntax

```cpp
priority_queue<int> pq;
```

Min Heap

```cpp
priority_queue<
int,
vector<int>,
greater<int>
> pq;
```

---

### Applications

- Dijkstra Algorithm
- Prim's Algorithm
- CPU Scheduling
- Event Simulation

---

# 6️⃣ C++ STL Queue

### Header

```cpp
#include <queue>
```

---

### Declaration

```cpp
queue<int> q;
```

---

### Operations

```cpp
q.push(10);

q.push(20);

q.pop();

q.front();

q.back();

q.empty();

q.size();
```

---

### Example

```cpp
#include<iostream>
#include<queue>
using namespace std;

int main()
{
    queue<int> q;

    q.push(10);

    q.push(20);

    q.push(30);

    cout << q.front();

    q.pop();

    cout << q.front();
}
```

---

# 📊 Complexity Summary

| Data Structure | Insert | Delete | Front |
|----------------|--------|--------|--------|
| Queue | O(1) | O(1) | O(1) |
